METHOD 3: InsertProductAsync
----------------------------------------
Lines: 130-198
SQL Statement Type: Multi-statement Transaction (INSERT + INSERT + UPDATE)
Changes Applied:
1. Removed DECLARE @NewProductId INT - managed at application level
2. Removed BEGIN TRANSACTION/COMMIT - managed at application level using BeginTransactionAsync/CommitAsync
3. SCOPE_IDENTITY() -> RETURNING ProductId clause on INSERT
4. GETDATE() -> NOW() (2 occurrences)
5. Split single multi-statement SQL into 3 separate SQL commands
6. Wrapped in try-catch with transaction management

Key Conversions:
- SQL Server: SCOPE_IDENTITY() + SET variable
- PostgreSQL: RETURNING ProductId (captured in C# code)

- SQL Server: GETDATE()
- PostgreSQL: NOW()

- SQL Server: BEGIN TRANSACTION ... COMMIT in SQL
- PostgreSQL: Application-level transaction using BeginTransactionAsync/CommitAsync

Implementation Notes:
- newProductId captured from RETURNING clause via ExecuteScalarAsync()
- Transaction managed at ADO.NET level for better error handling
- All parameters preserved (@Name, @Description, @Price, @StockQuantity)

Schema Object Changes: None

